Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 15:43:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] feat(web): pair only private LAN addresses and close the
 review polish

Keep the pairing form off a globally routable interface: the bundle derives
`pairingAddresses` as the RFC1918, link-local, and CGNAT subset of the sampled
literals, so an Internet client a public address admits through the fence never
receives the PIN form. The fence itself keeps every literal it always had.

Reject a `pairing.authorities` entry the fence cannot reach at load, naming the
misconfiguration, instead of serving a form whose every submission is a 403.
Report an exhausted process budget once on the console the operator reads.
Refuse to render the pairing page inside a frame, and share one request-header
reader between the fence and the browser-auth module.

The Agent Note and both READMEs record the private-only pairing subset, the
load-time fence rule, and that peer streaks are now bounded by the process
budget.
